				"⠃⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				125,
				5
			],
			"Message": "refactor(Grove): Extract Spine protocol types into directory module\n\nMove the Spine protocol constants, message types, configuration, error types, and unit tests out of the monolithic module hierarchy into a dedicated Source/Protocol/ directory. Each type gets its own file (Constants.rs, MessageType.rs, ProtocolConfig.rs, ProtocolError.rs, Tests.rs) following the crate's directory-based module convention.\n\nThis completes the ongoing Source-level atomization of the Grove crate, reducing inline-module bloat and establishing a clear protocol layer boundary for the Spine client-server interaction model.\n\n- Constants.rs: version string, default endpoint, timeouts, buffer sizes\n- MessageType.rs: typed Heartbeat/Register/Unregister/Event/Request/Response/Error enum with u32 round-trip conversion\n- ProtocolConfig.rs: builder-pattern config struct with Default impl\n- ProtocolError.rs: thiserror-based Connection/Serialization/InvalidMessage/Timeout/Protocol errors\n- Tests.rs: coverage for config defaults, builder overrides, and message type conversion",
			"SHA": "066dc998703457cca2e7c8f220742075904213a8"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-06-12T18:48:33Z",
			"File": [
				"⡟⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				120,
				18
			],
			"Message": "refactor(Grove): Atomize FunctionExport into directory module; standardize crate doc comments\n\nSplit the monolithic FunctionExport.rs (788 lines) into a directory-based module at Source/WASM/FunctionExport/ with dedicated files for HostFunctionRegistry, FunctionStats, ExportConfig, Default, and FunctionExportImpl, plus a re-exporting mod.rs. This completes the Source-level atomization work across the crate.\n\nStandardize doc comments across Common/Traits.rs, Common/mod.rs, API/Types.rs, Library.rs, and main.rs to use consistent period-terminated third-person descriptions aligned with Rust API doc convention. Replace bare //! header comments with \"# Module — Description\" format and convert Library.rs's flat module list to a markdown table for readability.\n\nFix ActivationEngine and ActivationHandler type paths to use qualified `Module::Struct` form (e.g. ActivationEvent::ActivationEvent::from_str), required after the prior Activation.rs and SpineActionClient atomization resolved E0573 naming ambiguities. Add a Debug implementation for MistTransport exposing its address and connection state. Relocate the Mist dependency from build-dependencies to the optional dependencies block for proper feature gating.",
			"SHA": "1e05787f79a9be892a67a3542aaa09c77e21c785"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-06-12T18:23:49Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				114,
				1
			],
			"Message": "feat(Grove): Auto-reconnect MistTransport on transport disconnect\n\nWire the recent Dial/Reconnect/LiveClient additions into the core MistTransport invoke and notify paths so that transient WebSocket drops are handled transparently rather than surfacing as errors.\n\n- **connect()** delegates to Dial() instead of inlining Client::connect(), unlocking MountainWebSocketSecret-based authentication via Mist's SharedSecret.\n- **invoke() and notify()** replace GetClient() with LiveClient(), which silently reconnects a stale connection before dispatching. On mid-request disconnect, both now catch the error, call Reconnect() with exponential backoff, and retry the call on the fresh client.\n\nCombined with the existing backoff loop in Reconnect(), this creates end-to-end resilience: every outgoing request either succeeds or exhausts the retry budget, without callers needing to manage connection state.",
			"SHA": "38c32f3de0bf8b36f402a5f93edf256eaa5003cd"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-06-12T18:20:40Z",
			"File": [
				"⡿⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				114,
				19
			],
			"Message": "refactor(Grove): Atomize Activation.rs into directory module; extract remaining SpineActionClient types; add Mist reconnect logic\n\n**Activation module atomization** — Split the monolithic Activation.rs (986 lines) into a dedicated Source/Host/Activation/ directory with seven focused files:\n\n- ActivationContext.rs: context data passed to extensions during activation\n- ActivationEvent.rs: typed activation event enum with from_str/to_string parsing\n- ActivationEngine.rs: core activation lifecycle (activate, deactivate, trigger, perform_activation with WASM dispatch)\n- ActivationHandler.rs: per-extension event handler tracking\n- ActivationRecord.rs: serializable activation history log\n- WildMatch.rs: simple wildcard pattern matching for activation events\n- Tests.rs: unit coverage for event parsing, context defaults, and wildcard matching\n\nThe original Activation.rs is retained as Activation.rs.bak for reference, then the mod.rs re-exports the new submodule hierarchy.\n\n**SpineActionClient type extraction** — Complete the atomization begun in the prior commit by moving the remaining inline structs, enums, and helper functions from the monolithic mod.rs into dedicated files:\n\n- ConnectionStatus.rs, GroveCapabilities.rs, HostInfo.rs, ReconnectStrategy.rs, SpineConfig.rs, calculate_backoff.rs, Tests.rs\n- mod.rs becomes a re-export hub referencing each sub-file\n- The primary client implementation remains in SpineActionClient.rs (renamed from mod.rs for structural consistency)\n\n**MistTransport reconnect resilience** — Add three methods and one utility function to the websocket block:\n\n- Dial(): opens a fresh Mist client, optionally authenticating with MountainWebSocketSecret via Mist's SharedSecret when present in the environment\n- Reconnect(): exponential-backoff retry loop (100/200/400/1000/2000 ms, 5 attempts), stores and returns the live client\n- LiveClient(): returns the stored client, transparently calling Reconnect() if the connection is detected as closed\n- IsDisconnect(): pattern-matches error strings to distinguish transport drops from server-side handler errors\n\nThese changes complete the Source/ module-level atomization and add production-grade reconnection to the Mist transport path.",
			"SHA": "75015ef4b0ae3c9c21ea1eff52e6401022ad7ea8"
		}
	],
